# =============================================================================
# bool-text-reject — a bare text ↦ bool aborts on an unknown word
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `textus ↦ bool` parses exactly the code locale's `true`/`false` words.
#   • With no `⊥` default, any other word is a run-time failure: the run
#     aborts with `text to bivalens conversion failed` and nothing prints
#     (operator ruling 2026-10-15, need).
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Expecting `"salve"` to be `true` — non-empty text is not truthiness.
#   • Omitting the `⊥` default when the input may be an arbitrary word.
#
# See also: ↦, bool — and the positive twin `bool-text.fab`.
# =============================================================================

main {
    print "salve" ↦ bool
}
